          "algorithm": "Select the next node by a weighted normalized sum of degree, betweenness, core number, and inverse clustering, with weights slightly adjusted for better balance between early disruption and final fragmentation.",
          "code": "def select_next_node(graph, unvisited_nodes):\n    import numpy as np\n    \n    degs = np.array([graph.nodes[n]['degree'] for n in unvisited_nodes], dtype=float)\n    bcs = np.array([graph.nodes[n]['betweenness'] for n in unvisited_nodes], dtype=float)\n    cores = np.array([graph.nodes[n]['core_number'] for n in unvisited_nodes], dtype=float)\n    clus = np.array([graph.nodes[n]['clustering'] for n in unvisited_nodes], dtype=float)\n    \n    def norm(arr):\n        mn, mx = arr.min(), arr.max()\n        return (arr - mn) / (mx - mn) if mx > mn else np.zeros_like(arr)\n    \n    degs_n = norm(degs)\n    bcs_n = norm(bcs)\n    cores_n = norm(cores)\n    inv_clus_n = norm(1 - clus)\n    \n    # Tweaked weights to slightly favor betweenness (early disruption) and core number (sustained fragmentation)\n    score = 0.3*degs_n + 0.4*bcs_n + 0.2*cores_n + 0.1*inv_clus_n\n    \n    idx = np.argmax(score)\n    return unvisited_nodes[idx]",
