          "algorithm": "Select the next node by scoring unvisited nodes with a weighted combination of normalized degree, betweenness, core number, and inverse clustering coefficient to balance immediate impact and long-term fragmentation.",
          "code": "def select_next_node(graph, unvisited_nodes):\n    import numpy as np\n    \n    degs = np.array([graph.nodes[n]['degree'] for n in unvisited_nodes], dtype=float)\n    bcs = np.array([graph.nodes[n]['betweenness'] for n in unvisited_nodes], dtype=float)\n    cores = np.array([graph.nodes[n]['core_number'] for n in unvisited_nodes], dtype=float)\n    clus = np.array([graph.nodes[n]['clustering'] for n in unvisited_nodes], dtype=float)\n    \n    # Normalize features to [0,1], handle constant arrays\n    def norm(arr):\n        mn, mx = arr.min(), arr.max()\n        return (arr - mn) / (mx - mn) if mx > mn else np.zeros_like(arr)\n    \n    degs_n = norm(degs)\n    bcs_n = norm(bcs)\n    cores_n = norm(cores)\n    # Use inverse clustering since low clustering often indicates bridge nodes\n    inv_clus = 1 - clus\n    inv_clus_n = norm(inv_clus)\n    \n    # Weights tuned to balance early disruption and final fragmentation\n    score = 0.35*degs_n + 0.35*bcs_n + 0.2*cores_n + 0.1*inv_clus_n\n    \n    idx = np.argmax(score)\n    return unvisited_nodes[idx]",
